💬 Done. Here's where each TODO item landed.

## 1. Cloud Run service account suffix — already done, verified not re-implemented

This was built on 2026-09-13/14. I verified it rather than taking plan.md's word:

- `.github/actions/gcp-auth/action.yml` puts the suffix on the address's **local part** (`udaan-deployer-prod@…`), and refuses an address that already carries one.
- The rule is **containment, not equality** — `git merge-base --is-ancestor` against `vars.PRODUCTION_BRANCH`. That matters because the trigger is a `v*` tag, and `refs/tags/v1.4.2` is never equal to `refs/heads/main`; equality would have sent every release to dev while reading fine in the diff.
- The suffix also covers the Cloud Run services, the migration job and the six Secret Manager entries — not just the account.

**One thing is still genuinely open and I could not close it from here:** `vars.PRODUCTION_BRANCH` defaults to `main`, and `git branch -a` confirms this repo has no `main` (only `development` and `master`, with just `origin/development` on the remote). So every release currently resolves to **dev** — loudly now, via a `::warning::`, but still dev. Setting that variable needs repository-settings access this sandbox doesn't have.

## 2. Pending items by priority — the ranked table had nothing implementable, so I used plan.md's own fallback

All eight ranked items are blocked on a decision, hardware, or GCP access. But plan.md prescribes a check against its own ranking: *grep for the gaps the repo's comments admit to*. That had worked twice out of two; it worked a third time.

**`AdminSchemeForm` was asking operators to paste a uuid under all four scopes**, justified by a comment saying no list route existed to pick a brand from. That was true when written and was falsified by `GET /admin/catalog/brands` — a change recorded elsewhere in plan.md as *closed*. Brand and category are now pickers; SKU and product stay pasted (a SKU has no route, and products are cursor-paginated, so a select over one page would be a sample presented as the catalog).

Two defects fell out that weren't the item:
- **Switching scope didn't clear the target**, and the submit sends only the current scope's field — so a brand uuid was posted as a `categoryId`. Free text hid it.
- **All four network-backed selects folded their error into the control's accessible name** by wrapping control and message in one `<label>` — a screen reader announcing "Brand, a brand-scoped scheme needs a brand, combo box", with the name changing as the error does. `TextField` had always done this correctly; the hand-rolled copies never took that half. Four copies is past `DeskSelect`'s own recorded trigger of three, so they're one `FormSelect` now and the fix landed once.

I also corrected **four false claims in `apps/web/README.md`** (operator surface "does not exist"; a design file deleted from the tree; wrong homes for `fetch` and `tokens.css`) and one in `jobs.module.ts`.

