💬 Done. Here's what happened across the three TODO items.

## 1. Cloud Run dev/prod service-account suffix — already implemented

This one needed verifying, not building. It landed on 2026-09-13/14 and is complete:

- `resolve` job answers `prod`/`dev` by **containment** in `vars.PRODUCTION_BRANCH` (default `main`), not ref-name equality — equality would send every `v*` tag to dev, since `refs/tags/v1.4.2` is never `refs/heads/main`.
- `.github/actions/gcp-auth` puts the suffix on the **local part** (`udaan-deployer-prod@…`), refuses a non-service-account address and one already carrying a suffix.
- The suffix also covers the Cloud Run services, the migration job and the twelve Secret Manager entries.
- `cloud-run-deploy.spec.ts` passes 17/17 and pins all of it.

**One thing to decide, and it's why this still costs you something:** this repo has no `main`. The branches are `development` and `master`, so the default resolves `no-branch` → dev on *every* release. The workflow now raises a `::warning::` naming the variable rather than failing silently, but until `vars.PRODUCTION_BRANCH` is set in repository settings, nothing can reach prod. I can't read or write repo variables from here — that's a one-setting change on your side.

## 2. Pending work by priority → plan.md item (18)

Of the open items, one was blocked on nothing. I took the cheapest, most-overlooked row: the signed-out screens.

They turned out not to be merely *unlisted* but **unreachable** — the harness seeds a session before every screen, and these nine are exactly the ones `RedirectIfSignedIn` sends away. Adding them as paths would have drawn the home screen nine more times and reported `/login` covered, which is the silent-green failure the harness exists to prevent. So a screen can now say `signedOut`, which buys a second browser context (`addInitScript` is per-context; there's no way to un-seed one page), with one shared route handler so the fixture matcher isn't duplicated.

**It found a real defect at the first drawing, matching the base rate plan.md predicts.** The Password / Phone OTP switch on `/login` measures **156 × 38** on the desk and **158 × 37** on the shop at 390px — under the 44px floor, on the first screen every operator and every shopkeeper sees, on the two buttons somebody who can't remember a password uses to reach the OTP. Both clients carry a byte-identical copy and *neither* had ever been floored — the twin problem in its first stage rather than its second. Fixed under `any-pointer: coarse` in both, with identically-worded spec rows so the next divergence shows in a diff. Both rows were checked against reverted sheets first (each fails), then re-rendered: **`target size` is now 0 on both clients**.

Two things plan.md and CLAUDE.md said about this row were wrong, and only opening the route tables showed it: there are **nine** screens across **two** clients, not eleven across three; and they don't all "read nothing" — both invitation screens preview their token, so without a fixture they'd draw a refusal branch and sweep clean. Both corrected.

## 3. plan.md updated

New item (20) with its narrative; (18) recounted (22/36 desk, 17/24 web); the harness-screen-list row struck through with its two errors recorded; item (1) sharpened (3.80:1 white-on-rust is now *every* primary action, including `Sign in`); item (2) annotated with the verification. I also ran the repo's own "grep for admitted gaps" check — it surfaced one genuinely untracked item, `client-core`'s eleven untested `format.ts` formatters, admitted in two config files and on no board. Filed as (21).

**Gates:** typecheck, lint, format, test (5403 across 358 suites) and build all pass. Final harness run on the committed state: 367 findings, admin 7, web 73, target size 0, all four fonts loaded, no unfixtured reads.

The 7 remaining desk findings are all item (17) — store/product names ellipsing in list tables — which is a recorded judgement, not a defect, and depends on how long real store names are. Nothing here has met a database, so I left it open rather than guessing.

