💬 All green. Here's where things landed.

## 1. Cloud Run service-account suffix — already implemented

This was done before this session. `resolve` answers `prod`/`dev` by **containment** in `vars.PRODUCTION_BRANCH` (not ref-name equality — the trigger is a `v*` tag, so equality would send every release to dev), and `.github/actions/gcp-auth` puts the suffix on the address's *local part*. `cloud-run-deploy.spec.ts` passes 17/17.

**One thing needs your decision, not code:** this repo has no `main` — branches are `development` and `master` — so on the default every release resolves to `dev`. The workflow now warns loudly about it, but `vars.PRODUCTION_BRANCH` has to be set in repository settings, which I can't reach from here.

## 2. Pending items by priority

Only two of the ten board items weren't blocked on a decision or hardware. Both are now closed.

**(18) — the render harness's screen list.** Added the last 15 screens with typed fixtures; the harness now draws **every leaf route on both clients** (36/36 desk, 23/23 shop). The `*` splats are excluded deliberately and that's written down, since an omission-by-decision is indistinguishable from an oversight from the sweep's side.

It found **7 real defects** — the base rate held, five batches for five:

- **`Call driver` at 88 × 32** — a `tel:` link, drawn only while a van is out, on the screen a shopkeeper opens *because* they want the driver, on the client that is a phone. Least defensible target in the repo.
- The saved list's `Remove` at **36 × 14** and `RENAME` at 46 × 14 — smallest targets on either client.
- `Delete this list` 87 × 31; the replenishment queue's Add 79 × 32 (the button that commits a purchase).
- The schemes list's `Retired` chip at **2.87:1** — this is `OrderStatusBadge`'s cancelled defect on its structural twin, including why the obvious repair is unavailable. `#fdf1ef` stopped being a literal and became `--color-accent-tint` on the way.

Re-rendered after: **target size 0 on both clients, 0 desk contrast, 0 unfixtured reads**, all four fonts confirmed loaded. Remaining findings are all pre-existing items (1), (17), (22).

**(21) — `format.ts`.** 11 untested formatters now covered, file at 100%, package 77.35 → 84.81. Writing it turned up that three formatters render in the *runner's* timezone — correct in the product, a trap in a spec, since this sandbox is UTC and every developer of this product isn't. Also two wrong examples in `format.ts`'s own comments: `3 Sep` renders `3 Sept` (CLDR data — recorded, and all date assertions moved to March so a September row can't go red on one leg of CI's Node matrix), and `3 Sep, 7–11am` isn't a shape `DeliverySlot` can produce at all — that one fixed. Caught by `tsc`, not vitest.

## 3. plan.md updated

Both items struck through with what they returned; new § "The formatters"; the harness screen list closed; counts corrected (`apps/web` had **six** screens left, not five — third time a count about that list was wrong).

I also ran the admissions grep the board recommends. **It came back empty — first miss in eight attempts**, and I recorded that rather than omitting it: the sweep finds gaps somebody *wrote down*, so it goes quiet exactly when that backlog is worked off. All seven of (18)'s defects were in screens no comment anywhere had flagged.

**Verification discipline:** every new spec row was checked against a deliberately broken copy — 6 style rows fail one-for-one, the timezone rows fail exactly 2 when the local-midnight parse is reverted. Four gates pass: typecheck, lint, format, **5435 tests across 358 suites**, build.

**Not verified here:** anything needing a database, Docker, or GCP — unchanged from the standing list.

